A||||15||JBGehling||Bra= good or bad?||||5||
Z||000000||JBGehling||10-31-2000||05:58 PM||||Hello again,<BR>    I just stumbled upon my dad's bra for the '88 GT that he recently passed down to me. The bra is not the ones that I usually see on here as it goes past the headlights (a pain in the a** at night) and it has a huge fiero pegasus on it. After I put it on and drove it around for a couple days, I found that when I took it off, a good deal of sand had collected underneath it. There were no scratches on the car, but I'm still a little hesitant to put something on it that collects sand. So here's the question... has anyone owned the bra that I'm talking about AND the small bra that doesn't go above the headlights? And, if so, does the smaller one collect less dirt (because I really like the look of a bra (no pun intended  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">....))? Also, does anyone know what speeds the bras at <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com</A>  are made for? (or is it all speeds?).<BR>Thanks in advance, <BR>Josh||||reg||5
Z||000001||stsmithgt||10-31-2000||06:16 PM||||I have a Colgan bra w/o the peggy on it.  It goes past the lights and IS a pain to roll up the light covers AND to get into the front trunk.  I don't seem to have the trouble of getting sand in my bra.  Is the big guy on the beach kicking sand in your face? J/K  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I have had typical dirty residue build up if I leave it on a week or so.  I live near the beach too.  Getting onto highway 1, I'm sure I kick up sand all the time.  sometimes I slide through it on the on ramp.  I wouldn't wear the bra on a windy day though.  Sand gets in EVERTHING no matter what you do. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Well that's my 2 cents...or a nickle.||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||10-31-2000||06:27 PM||||Todd, you really look silly wearing the bra -- (if I keep this up maybe I can blackmail you into giving me the steering wheel?)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                           <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT<BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group<BR><A HREF="http://www.http://www.fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>www.http://www.fieroshop.net/</A> - Fiero Shop - Richmond, CA - 1-510-23-FIERO||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||10-31-2000||06:56 PM||||I'm looking into buying the blue GT that Doug has for sale.  Since the paint is slightly messed up on the front fascia and I'll repaint the entire car someday, I don't mind if I get some dirt under a bra.  Anyone have pics of both styles??  What's the best place to get either style?||||reg||1
Z||000004||TwisT||10-31-2000||07:26 PM||||...Have had lot's of experience with different bras on different vehicles.  They work great to protect against paint chips/ scratches but ONLY if frequently removed and cleaned thoroughly.  Any dirt left behind can mess up your paint pronto.<P>Something else I've experienced...  make sure the bra does not flap in the wind;  this will scuff your paint real quick.<P>Cheers,<P>Brett<BR>Yankton,  SD||||reg||1
Z||000005||wkayl||10-31-2000||08:06 PM||||Hey there Brett.  I "hear" that at 110 mph they will come loose and flap when you pass a truck someplace between Mission and Murdo.  I grew up near Aberdeen and my Wife is from Sisseton so we make that trip 5 or 6 times a year.  My Fiero has made the 1,400 mile round trip about 4 times in the last 2 years.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fieroboy1||10-31-2000||08:06 PM||||I used to have a bra on my old 87 SE from the fiero store, the smaller style below the lights.  It is made by wolf.  I've had that car up around 110 with no problems...4cyl mind you so it wasn't that easy...lol  But bras are made to conceal damage in my book, they are way to much work to put on nice paint because you have to constantly remove and wax the area covered.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tigger||10-31-2000||11:41 PM||||If I ever bought a bra for mine, it would have to be one of those tiger striped ones.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Opps, nevermind...<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000008||deceler8||11-01-2000||09:58 AM||||I used to be a Bra fan, liking the way they looked, until one night I was driving to BG from Toledo and the damn thing flew off in a rainstorm. Never found it.<P>And never had much luck with LeBra's either. The elastic tends to wear out making the thing sag.||||reg||1
Z||000009||stsmithgt||11-01-2000||10:35 AM||||Hey when I wear a bra... I mean when my CAR wears a bra, It can go 115 mph without any bra trouble.  I don't remeber if I had the headlight covers rolled up or not.  I think they were down.(Colgan type bra)<P>HEY Terry <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  If I don't get back in better shape, I might need a bra in a few years. hah!  I'm working out by hanging on to my steering wheel real hard..HE he||||reg||12
Z||000010||Spyder||11-01-2000||05:10 PM||||Here is my old Fiero Gt Bra: <BR>Sorry this one covers the head lights.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Bra.jpg"> <BR>I know that I have posted this before, but this is fot the new guys.<P>A bra is only good if you have a saggy front.||||reg||12
