Z||000012||Madrox86GT||11-01-2000||11:08 PM||||well i have taken a good through look at Jammers blue w/ white racing stripes 4 cyl. and it is SUPER except fro the front nose....it had a bra on it he said and the guy who he got it form hit something and when he took the bra off the paint is chippend every where down to the gray....but i was thinking i could get a bra back on it till i re-paint. good idea?<P>------------------<BR>You know my saying is:<P>"life is  a  B I T C H... then you marry one."<P>-Red 84 SE for parts(or 300 all together)-<BR>-Trade/Sell 86 GT-<BR>-New Pioneer Raido and 4X10's-<P>-Silver V6 SE(wrecked) $300<BR>-Black 85 coupe(parts car)$500<BR>-or both black and sliver for $750||||reg||1
Z||000013||olympic||11-02-2000||12:08 AM||||I agree with TwisT 100%.   You have to be almost anal about keeping dirt and water out from under the bra.  If it gets wet and then sits in the sun you get mildew.  And if it flops in the wind it will scratch up the paint.  You can also get strange fade marks if your car sits in the sun alot.<P>  But if your front fascia is all broken or scratcherd up already then you have nothing to lose!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
